    "Reduced effect (~%@)" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Efecto reducido (~%@)"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "效应减弱（约 %@）"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "效應減弱（約 %@）"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Reduces central nervous system excitability, typically through enhancement of inhibitory GABAergic neurotransmission and/or reduction of excitatory glutamatergic neurotransmission. Produces sedation, anxiolysis, and muscle relaxation in a dose-dependent manner." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Reduce la excitabilidad del sistema nervioso central, normalmente potenciando la neurotransmisión GABAérgica inhibitoria y/o disminuyendo la neurotransmisión glutamatérgica excitatoria. Produce sedación, ansiólisis y relajación muscular de forma dependiente de la dosis."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "降低中枢神经系统兴奋性，通常通过增强抑制性 GABA 能神经传递和/或减少兴奋性谷氨酸能神经传递。以剂量依赖的方式产生镇静、抗焦虑和肌肉松弛。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "降低中樞神經系統興奮性，通常透過增強抑制性 GABA 能神經傳導和/或減少興奮性麩胺酸能神經傳導。以劑量依賴的方式產生鎮靜、抗焦慮和肌肉鬆弛。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Reduces pain perception through mechanisms that may include inhibition of prostaglandin synthesis, activation of endogenous opioid pathways, modulation of descending pain inhibitory circuits, or blockade of peripheral nociceptor sensitization. The specific mechanism depends on the drug class." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Disminuye la percepción del dolor mediante mecanismos que pueden incluir la inhibición de la síntesis de prostaglandinas, la activación de vías opioides endógenas, la modulación de los circuitos descendentes inhibitorios del dolor o el bloqueo de la sensibilización de los nociceptores periféricos. El mecanismo concreto depende de la clase de fármaco."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "通过抑制前列腺素合成、激活内源性阿片通路、调节下行性痛觉抑制环路或阻断外周伤害感受器敏化等机制减少痛觉。具体机制取决于药物类别。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "透過抑制前列腺素合成、活化內源性鴉片通路、調節下行性痛覺抑制環路或阻斷周邊傷害感受器敏化等機制減少痛覺。具體機制取決於藥物類別。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Reference" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Referencia"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "参考文献"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
